	(descr "Micras wall joint: the main board's side of the joint with a wall-sensor board (boards/wall), whose 2x03 1.27 mm header (HX PZ1.27-2x3P ZZ) straddles its bottom edge: 6 plated holes, 0.70 mm drill (drawing: 0.65 mm) and 1.10 mm pads at 1.27 x 1.27 mm, pad n = header pin n; origin on the pattern's centre, under the wall board's mid-plane, the sensor looking along -y. F.CrtYd: the header's insulator, on which the wall board's 4.2 mm handle stands, plus 0.25 mm; F.Fab: the 8.4 mm blade's overhang with its back-face parts, 3.06 mm or more over the board outside the courtyard, under which parts stay at or below 2.55 mm")
